      "description": "The arbitrary sentence functions K and F need not arise from the syntax of L_EA. In particular, Lean does not require F φ to be obtained from a single one-free-variable formula by substituting the numeral for the Gödel number of φ; it models neither that coding nor object-language quantification."
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Apart from the declared proviso, the pointwise hypothesis and conclusion match Theorem 4, including the scope of provability and the nesting of K, on the reading Con(F) = ¬F(⊥). The proviso restricts the result to F for which the base proves F(Con(F)) → F(⊥), so this is not the unrestricted printed theorem."
